    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of every validation and side-effect applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, backed by `OwnerFieldsDto` and `ClinicServiceImpl`).\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else `AccessDeniedException` (403).\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`), all enforced before any controller code; failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 **400**:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words with space/`'`/`-`)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` (must contain non-whitespace)\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (must contain non-whitespace)\n   - `postcode` (nullable): `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email` (nullable): `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`\n   - `registrationDate` (nullable): `@Valid`\n   - (`sharesHousehold` has no constraints and is **not** mapped onto the entity \u2014 effectively ignored)\n\n## Inside the controller body, in code order\n\n3. **Map** DTO \u2192 `Owner` (new entity, `id == null`; `sharesHousehold` dropped by the mapper).\n4. **Normalize address** (trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand `ST`/`RD`/`AVE`); if the result is empty \u2192 **400**. Normalized value is stored back.\n5. **Email normalization/validation** \u2014 only if email present: trim + lowercase, then check against `^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$`; invalid \u2192 **400**. Normalized value stored back.\n6. **Postcode-vs-city/region check** (`isPostcodeValidForCity`: 4-digit postcode within the city's allowed regional range); invalid \u2192 **400**.\n7. **Telephone normalization** to E.164 (`^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`, with national-number-length rules); invalid/null result \u2192 **400**. Normalized value stored back.\n8. **Resolve registration date** \u2014 default to `LocalDate.now()` if absent, then roll any weekend forward to Monday (business-day). Stored back onto the owner.\n9. **Per-day cap** \u2014 if owners already registered on that date `>= 100` \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.\n10. **Compute & set identity key**; **duplicate check** (`isDuplicate`) \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n11. **Per-city cap** \u2014 if owners in that city `>= 50` \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n12. **Assign registration attributes** (`assignRegistrationAttributes`) \u2014 side-effect on the entity: sets `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, `householdId` (SHA-256 based), `namesakeCount`, `householdMemberCount`, `membershipLevel`. These are computed from the current owner population, so they run before the save.\n13. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (`@Transactional`) \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (JPA persist). At flush/commit the **entity-level constraints** are validated (`Owner`/`Person`: `@NotEmpty` firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone, `@Pattern` postcode `^[0-9]{4}$`, `@Pattern` telephone E.164). The DB assigns the generated `id`.\n14. **Audit log** (success only) \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` records id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n15. **Map** entity \u2192 `OwnerDto`; set `bulkSignupWarning` (true if >80 owners created today).\n16. **Set `Location` header** \u2192 `/api/owners/{id}`.\n17. **Return 201 CREATED** with the owner body.\n\n## Notes on transactions and ordering\n\n- The controller is **not** `@Transactional`. Each helper's `findAllOwners()` (used by the per-day cap, duplicate check, per-city cap, attribute assignment, and bulk-signup warning) and the final `saveOwner()` each run in their **own** transaction (reads are `readOnly`, the save is read-write). So all the count/duplicate checks (steps 9\u201311) execute in separate read transactions before the write.\n- No application events, emails, or notifications are published anywhere on this path \u2014 the only side-effects are the entity mutations (steps 4,5,7,8,10,12), the DB insert (13), and the audit log line (14).\n- Relevant exception handling (`ExceptionControllerAdvice`): bean-validation failures \u2192 400, `DataIntegrityViolationException` \u2192 404, `AccessDeniedException` \u2192 rethrown (403), other exceptions \u2192 500."
